menu "Example Configuration"

    config ML_EXAMPLE_TARGET_PEER_IP
        string "Target Peer VPN IP (for sending)"
        default ""
        help
            VPN IP of the peer to send "hello" messages to (e.g., "100.103.181.24").
            Leave empty to only receive (no outgoing messages).
            The peer should run: nc -lu 9000

    config ML_EXAMPLE_LIFECYCLE_CYCLES
        int "Stop/start lifecycle test cycles (0 = disabled)"
        default 0
        range 0 1000
        help
            After the first connection, run this many microlink_stop() /
            microlink_start() cycles before entering the normal loop. The
            cycles rotate through three variants:
              - stop after CONNECTED, then start the same handle
              - stop 3 s after start (mid-registration / MapResponse, so
                the control-plane task is blocked in a socket read)
              - stop + microlink_destroy() + microlink_init() + start
            Each cycle logs "LIFECYCLE n/N" lines with the stop duration and
            free heap; the run ends with "LIFECYCLE RESULT: PASS" or "FAIL".
            Also set CONFIG_LOG_MAXIMUM_LEVEL_DEBUG=y to get an "ml_heap"
            line with the free internal RAM after each teardown step.
            Leave at 0 for normal use.

endmenu
